      "note": "One monumental Baroque composition by Willem De Bruyn (1696-1698) across Grand-Place 13-19. The City dataset gives the same base facade description for 14-19, varying only the house emblem, and records the site as 'already unified brick houses from 1441'. Record 014 (Grand-Place 13) states it has no facade of its own because it sits inside the block. Treat this group as ONE facade unit: an image of the composition is not a facade observation for any single house. Commons files the seven houses as Renommée (13), Ermitage (14), Fortune (15), Moulin à vent (16), Pot d'étain (17), Colline (18) and Bourse (19), each carrying a Brussels monument record 2043-0065/013-019. City record 014 (Grand-Place 13) is named 'Fortune', which is Grand-Place 15; the monument record for Grand-Place 13 is Maison de la Renommée. The City name is not corrected here, only recorded."
    },
